  "problem": "What is the equation of the *horizontal* asymptote of the function $y=-\\frac{1}{x}?$\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=-\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14230521/assets/400dad20519cecf16db43999fd18787643040023135f9e45b0b9f81a98d3717f.png)\n\nNotice that $y\\to 0$ as $x\\to \\infty .$ Therefore, the equation of the horizontal asymptote is $y=0.$",
